2090: sweetfb_barcheck=1 samples each frame's slot right before the flip for dark bars, classifies them against the source surface, and checks the two display invariants on the device (a slot is never written while scanned, a source never changes during its copy). Boot-arg off: one bool test per present. UNTESTED ON A PHONE, syntax-checked with the kernel's flags, scan logic host-tested by plans/blackbars/test/bar-test.c.
What it prints: see analysis/blackbars.md. Grep "SWEET FB BAR:".
Apply: git apply after 2053, then rebuild the kernel. Reads only; no display behaviour changes.

